# Completion report: build-minion-town-inference-phase3-secrets

I opened draft PR **https://github.com/kriscendobot/minion.town/pull/183**. It holds the Endo pin bump, Claude credentials on the daemon's `@secrets`, and a prompt-origin gate on the root user's backend. CI is green (`test`, `Claude harness (amd64)`, `Claude harness (arm64)`). It sits on head `build/inference-phase3-secrets` against frozen base `main-bc11010`, a snapshot of `main` I created because `ensure-pr.sh` requires one.

## What changed

**1. Endo pin moved to `llm@204033b398`.** All four copies moved together: `ENDO_COMMIT` in `deploy-endo-daemon.sh`, `PINNED_ENDO_COMMIT` in `root-host-socket.ts`, the CI checkout ref, and `vendor/endo-claude` (refreshed with `tools/vendor-endo-claude.sh`).
- **Daemon risk is low.** Between the old pin `1706e63247` and the new one, the daemon changes in only seven files, with no database or migration change. A missing migration is what crash-looped prod on the #104/#110 bump.
- **Checked against a real daemon.** I installed an Endo checkout at the new pin and ran the full live-daemon suite against it: 9/9 pass, including a new secrets test. CI's `test` job runs the same suite against the same pin and also passes.
- **One vendoring workaround.** Upstream `@endo/claude`'s entry file now also exports code that imports `@endo/agent-mcp-stdio`, which isn't published. The vendor tool now cuts that trailing block from the entry file and its type file, and records the cut text word for word in `PROVENANCE.json` (`removedTail`). The vendor test still checks every file against its upstream copy.

**2. Credentials on `@secrets`** (new `src/endo/claude/secrets-credential-vault.ts`, wired in through `cli-deployment.ts`).
- **Storage:** the `setup-token` capture now stores each subject's token through the root host's `@secrets/create`. The record is named `claude-<hash>` and its description includes `kind=subscription`, so the credential kind is stored with it.
- **Changes:** capturing a new token replaces the stored value in place; disconnecting revokes and then deletes the record.
- **What stays on disk:** only state with no token in it (plan models, when it was stored, whether the confinement probe passed).
- **Old records:** a record written by the old file store, with the token inline, moves onto `@secrets` the first time it is read and is rewritten without the token.
- **Test:** a new live-daemon test covers storing, pending until activated, replacing, revoking and that migration.

**3. Prompt-origin gate** (new `src/endo/claude/prompt-origin-gate.ts`).
- **Placement:** it wraps the production root backend in `cli-deployment.ts`. It behaves like `@endo/inference`'s `makePromptOriginGate`: any prompt not labelled root-authored is refused before the backend runs.
- **Labelling:** an agent's remotely callable `infer` labels every prompt guest-influenced. Only the root user's own MCP `infer` tool reaches the root-authored path, so another holder of an agent can't claim root authorship.
- **Refusals** return `{type:"error", reason:"needs-containment"}` and are logged. That reuses an existing result type, so no caller needed a new case. New unit tests are in `test/claude-prompt-origin-gate.test.ts`.
- **Behaviour change:** inbox responders and mailed delegations on the root's backend are now refused. That matches the design until the sandboxed backend (design phase 6) and gate 8 exist.

`DEPLOYMENT.md` is updated for the new credential storage and the gate. `ENDO_CLAUDE_ENABLED` and `minion-mcp.service` are unchanged, and no new production traffic is enabled. I did **not** run the root canary or gate 1; those stay with the parked `minion-town-claude-kriscendobot-canary-after-connect-20261006`.

